WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:06.623
Just then Alpha began ringing.

2
00:00:06.624 --> 00:00:10.034
"Shh," Ally said. "I'm trying to think!"

3
00:00:10.035 --> 00:00:14.436
"Illogical response," Alpha said. "You have a phone call."

4
00:00:14.437 --> 00:00:17.634
"Oh!" Ally pushed the talk button.

5
00:00:17.635 --> 00:00:22.171
"Hello?" Mateo huffed on the other end.

6
00:00:22.172 --> 00:00:24.747
"Mateo, are you all right?"

7
00:00:24.748 --> 00:00:28.622
"Yes," Mateo replied breathlessly.

8
00:00:28.623 --> 00:00:34.292
"I tried to follow the limo on my bike, but I lost it. Are you all right?"

9
00:00:34.293 --> 00:00:38.433
"Not really!" Ally explained everything.

10
00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:43.097
"Don't worry. I'll get the meld medallion back from her," Mateo said.

11
00:00:43.098 --> 00:00:47.593
"Have Alpha send me your location. I'll be there as fast as I can!"

12
00:00:47.594 --> 00:00:54.143
While Ally waited for Mateo, she crept out of the bathroom to check out the P.O.D.'s technology.

13
00:00:54.144 --> 00:00:59.989
"Nothing here looks super advanced." Ally inspected the P.O.D.'s control panel.

14
00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:03.942
"Carparians are known to be exceptional engineers.

15
00:01:03.943 --> 00:01:06.204
Maybe Lainie is human after all.

16
00:01:06.205 --> 00:01:10.607
Still, I can't be sure until I see her with the meld medallion on."

17
00:01:10.608 --> 00:01:13.695
Ally finished her inspection.

18
00:01:13.696 --> 00:01:18.435
She'd just returned to the bathroom when someone burst into the P.O.D.

19
00:01:18.436 --> 00:01:21.035
"I'm here!" Mateo cried.

20
00:01:21.036 --> 00:01:25.986
"I've got good news and bad news. Which do you want first?"

21
00:01:25.987 --> 00:01:30.472
Ally stepped out of the bathroom. "The good news!"

22
00:01:30.473 --> 00:01:37.185
"Here's your medallion!" Mateo said.

23
00:01:37.186 --> 00:01:39.419
"Lainie was wearing it when I got here.

24
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.708
She looked like herself, not a Carparian.

25
00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:45.540
And she was so distracted by angry bird-watchers,

26
00:01:45.541 --> 00:01:52.894
she barely paid attention when I asked her if I could look at her unusual necklace."

27
00:01:52.895 --> 00:02:00.021
"Phew!" Ally slipped it on. "Angry bird-watchers? I thought they were reporters out there."

28
00:02:00.022 --> 00:02:03.458
"That's the bad news," Mateo replied.

29
00:02:03.459 --> 00:02:06.722
"Those bird-watchers found the whoopers' nest."

30
00:02:06.723 --> 00:02:10.486
"Huh? Why is that bad news?"

31
00:02:10.487 --> 00:02:15.435
"You'd better come with me." Mateo led Ally out of the P.O.D.

32
00:02:15.436 --> 00:02:20.026
As he'd said, Lainie was surrounded by bird-watchers.

33
00:02:20.027 --> 00:02:23.434
"Why are they so angry?" Ally asked.

34
00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:29.481
Mateo pointed to the top of the P.O.D. "The whoopers' nest is up there!"

35
00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.204
Ally gasped.

36
00:02:32.205 --> 00:02:36.293
"They're just birds!" Lainie said.

37
00:02:36.294 --> 00:02:41.282
"They could be the last whoopers in the world!" a bird-watcher shouted back.

38
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:48.796
"If they don't successfully hatch these eggs, the species could go extinct."

39
00:02:48.797 --> 00:02:54.866
"Well, then I'll build a statue to their memory," Lainie said.

40
00:02:54.867 --> 00:02:58.593
That made the bird-watchers even angrier.

41
00:02:58.594 --> 00:03:01.660
Ally hurried over. "Now, now, everyone.

42
00:03:01.661 --> 00:03:07.755
I know we can resolve this peacefully. Bird-watchers, what do you want?"

43
00:03:07.756 --> 00:03:11.018
"That nest can't be moved," one said.

44
00:03:11.019 --> 00:03:17.782
"We want Lainie to delay the flight until the eggs have hatched, and the babies are big enough to leave the nest."

45
00:03:17.783 --> 00:03:26.117
"But that will take three months!" Lainie moaned.

46
00:03:26.118 --> 00:03:28.105
Ally turned to her.

47
00:03:28.106 --> 00:03:34.921
"There's no point in exploring other planets if we don't do everything we can to save the planet we're on."

48
00:03:34.922 --> 00:03:37.232
The bird-watchers cheered.

49
00:03:37.233 --> 00:03:38.327
"She's right!"

50
00:03:38.328 --> 00:03:41.413
"Listen to her!"

51
00:03:41.414 --> 00:03:50.248
Lainie sighed. "Fine. We should help the birds. I'll delay the launch."

52
00:03:50.249 --> 00:04:01.102
The bird-watchers cheered louder.

53
00:04:01.103 --> 00:04:08.497
"Guess I'll see you in three months, Ally," Lainie said as she started back to her limo.

54
00:04:08.498 --> 00:04:13.298
"And let me know if you ever want to sell that necklace."

55
00:04:13.299 --> 00:04:19.664
Ally nodded and waved good-bye.

56
00:04:19.665 --> 00:04:24.575
"Wow, Ally," Mateo said. "That was really kind of you.

57
00:04:24.576 --> 00:04:29.085
You could have gone home, but you chose to save the whoopers."

58
00:04:29.086 --> 00:04:32.738
Ally shrugged. "I can wait three months.

59
00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:37.756
This way I'll have more time to convince your mom to stay in Sandville."

60
00:04:37.757 --> 00:04:43.342
Mateo grinned. "Sounds good to me!"

61
00:04:43.343 --> 00:04:47.930
But when they got back to Ray's house, Dawn's suitcases were gone.

62
00:04:47.931 --> 00:04:54.934
"I've failed!" Ally moaned. She sat on the couch, her head in her hands.

63
00:04:54.935 --> 00:05:02.327
Mateo looked miserable too, until a minute later, when Ray and Dawn walked in, laughing.

64
00:05:02.328 --> 00:05:05.666
"I'm glad you're here, Mateo," Dawn said.

65
00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:09.370
"I wanted to tell you that I've decided to go back to the city.

66
00:05:09.371 --> 00:05:12.680
You and your dad will stay here."

67
00:05:12.681 --> 00:05:15.857
"I don't understand," Ally burst out.

68
00:05:15.858 --> 00:05:19.617
"If you love each other, then why not stay together?

69
00:05:19.618 --> 00:05:24.112
Opening a shop here is the perfect solution!"

70
00:05:24.113 --> 00:05:27.250
"Things aren't always that simple," Dawn said.

71
00:05:27.251 --> 00:05:30.757
"We love each other, but we want different things.

72
00:05:30.758 --> 00:05:36.938
I want to be in the city for my career, and Ray's life is here with the diner.

73
00:05:36.939 --> 00:05:40.776
Mateo, you are the most important thing to us.

74
00:05:40.777 --> 00:05:47.595
Even when we aren't together, we will always be a family."

75
00:05:47.596 --> 00:05:50.292
Ally watched Mateo hug his parents.

76
00:05:50.293 --> 00:05:58.714
Then Ray reached for her. "You're part of our family too, Ally."

77
00:05:58.715 --> 00:06:03.778
"I guess there are all kinds of families," she thought, hugging all of them.

78
00:06:03.779 --> 00:06:06.848
"And families don't all have to look the same."

79
00:06:06.849 --> 00:06:18.866
After all, her parents were her Astralian family, and Ray and Mateo were her Earth family—at least for three more months!

